  "notes": "A compound of {摩|ま} (to rub, to grind) and {耗|もう} (to wear out, to diminish). Primarily a technical term used for physical wear on materials and machinery.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {摩耗|まもう}が{激|はげ}しい (severely worn)\n- {摩耗|まもう}に{強|つよ}い (resistant to wear)\n- {摩耗|まもう}{防止|ぼうし} (wear prevention)\n- タイヤの{摩耗|まもう} (tire wear)\n- {経年|けいねん}{摩耗|まもう} (wear from aging)\n\nAlso written as {磨耗|まもう} with the alternate kanji {磨|ま}. Both writings are common.",
